# Cursor Rules for Multi WhatsApp Web Instance Manager

## Code Change Workflow

**IMPORTANT: Every time code is changed or edited, follow this exact sequence:**

### 1. Commit to GitHub
- Stage all changes: `git add -A`
- Commit with descriptive message: `git commit -m "Description of changes"`
- Push to GitHub: `git push origin main`

### 2. Push to Server (Pull on Server)
- SSH to server: `ssh -i LightsailDefaultKey-ap-southeast-3.pem ubuntu@108.137.37.171`
- Navigate to project: `cd ~/wa-web`
- Pull latest code: `git pull origin main`

**OR use one-liner:**
```bash
ssh -i LightsailDefaultKey-ap-southeast-3.pem ubuntu@108.137.37.171 "cd ~/wa-web && git pull origin main"
```

### 3. Compile Frontend (if frontend code changed)
**Only if changes were made to files in `frontend/` directory:**
- SSH to server: `ssh -i LightsailDefaultKey-ap-southeast-3.pem ubuntu@108.137.37.171`
- Navigate to frontend: `cd ~/wa-web/frontend`
- Install dependencies (if needed): `npm install`
- Build frontend: `npm run build`
- Copy to public: `cd ~/wa-web && mkdir -p public && cp -r frontend/dist/* public/`

**OR use one-liner:**
```bash
ssh -i LightsailDefaultKey-ap-southeast-3.pem ubuntu@108.137.37.171 "cd ~/wa-web/frontend && npm run build && cd .. && mkdir -p public && cp -r frontend/dist/* public/"
```

### 4. Restart Service
- SSH to server: `ssh -i LightsailDefaultKey-ap-southeast-3.pem ubuntu@108.137.37.171`
- Restart service: `sudo systemctl restart wa-web.service`
- Check status: `sudo systemctl status wa-web.service --no-pager`

**OR use one-liner:**
```bash
ssh -i LightsailDefaultKey-ap-southeast-3.pem ubuntu@108.137.37.171 "sudo systemctl restart wa-web.service && sleep 2 && sudo systemctl status wa-web.service --no-pager | head -15"
```

### 5. Update Documentation
- Update relevant documentation files in `docs/` directory
- If new feature: Add to `docs/features/`
- If API change: Update `docs/api/API-DOCUMENTATION.md`
- If deployment change: Update `docs/deployment/`
- Commit documentation: `git add docs/ && git commit -m "Update documentation" && git push`

## Quick Deployment Script

For convenience, use the deployment script:
```bash
cd "/Users/danielbudiono/cursor_projects/multi wa whatwappwebjs"
ssh -i LightsailDefaultKey-ap-southeast-3.pem ubuntu@108.137.37.171 "cd ~/wa-web && bash scripts/deploy.sh"
```

## Server Information

- **Server IP**: 108.137.37.171
- **SSH User**: ubuntu
- **SSH Key**: `LightsailDefaultKey-ap-southeast-3.pem` (in project root)
- **Project Path**: `/home/ubuntu/wa-web`
- **Service Name**: `wa-web.service`

## File Change Detection

**Frontend changes** (require compilation):
- Any file in `frontend/src/`
- `frontend/package.json`
- `frontend/vite.config.js`
- `frontend/tailwind.config.js`

**Backend changes** (require service restart only):
- `server.js`
- Any file in `src/`
- `package.json` (root)
- Database migrations in `database/migrations/`

**Both** (require compilation + restart):
- Changes to both frontend and backend files

## Commit Message Guidelines

- Use clear, descriptive commit messages
- Include what was changed and why
- Format: `"Action: Description of changes"`
- Examples:
  - `"Fix: Statistics periods refresh after settings save"`
  - `"Add: Statistics feature with unreplied customer tracking"`
  - `"Update: Deploy script to include database migration"`

## Notes

- Always verify service status after restart
- Check logs if service fails: `sudo journalctl -u wa-web.service -n 50`
- Frontend build takes ~10-15 seconds
- Service restart takes ~2-3 seconds
- Always test changes locally before deploying

